  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_patchify(images: list, patch_size: int = 2) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **ViT Patchify** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_patchify(images: list, patch_size: int = 2) -> list:\n    img = np.array(images, dtype=np.float64)\n    if img.ndim == 3: img = img[np.newaxis, :, :, :]\n    B, C, H, W = img.shape; p = int(patch_size); nh, nw = H // p, W // p\n    res = []\n    for b in range(B):\n        res.append([np.transpose(img[b, :, i*p:(i+1)*p, j*p:(j+1)*p], (1, 2, 0)).flatten().tolist() for i in range(nh) for j in range(nw)])\n    return np.round(res, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
